window.docContents[216].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalE2E.SchemeModel/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalE2E___SchemeModel":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalE2E › SchemeModel.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 20 of 167 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nFixed Two-Party Configuration and SPQR-Off Session OutcomesTrusted in part. Computational/Theorems/ uses serializedPartyAddresses, partyDeviceId, partyIdentityKeyBytes, partyIdentityKey, and partyAddressName; spqrOffSessionParams, initKeysE, Reach, sendModelSpqrOff, and recvModelSpqrOff are checked by Lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md and Computational/docs/DEVIATIONS.md (DEV-M3, DEV-M4, DEV-M5, DEV-M10, DEV-E8).\n\n\n\nThe parties (constants of the image)\n\ndef partyAddressNameL37–45 ↗#The protocol address name of each party: a fixed hyphenated UUID.DEV-M3 (libsignal): the parties' addresses are constants. ACD19 Def. 6 has two parties A and B and no addresses. libsignal MACs both parties' addresses, and the wrapper fixes them: these two UUID names and device 1 (partyDeviceId). Why: the image is one fixed configuration. Effect: w.l.o.g., argued: the session model's bound holds for every address blob.\n\n2 declarations not shown (lines 47–69): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.E2E.partyIdentityKeyBytes, CryptoVerification.E2E.partyIdentityKey\n\ndef partyDeviceIdL71–72 ↗#Every party uses device 1.\n\ndef serializedPartyAddressesL74–82 ↗#serialize_addresses(sender, recipient) of the two parties' addresses (names partyAddressName, device 1) under the UUID parser uuidParse: none if a name does not parse (then libsignal MACs without addresses, in the binary and in the session model alike). The scheme uses it at the trusted model uuidTryParse of Uuid::try_parse (spqrOffSessionParams), under which both names parse.\n\n5 declarations not shown (lines 86–165): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.E2E.spqrOffSessionParams, CryptoVerification.E2E.initKeysE, CryptoVerification.E2E.Reach.recv, CryptoVerification.E2E.Reach.send, CryptoVerification.E2E.Reach, CryptoVerification.E2E.Reach.initB, CryptoVerification.E2E.Reach.initA, CryptoVerification.E2E.sendModelSpqrOff, CryptoVerification.E2E.recvModelSpqrOff\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalE2E/SchemeModel.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalE2E.SchemeModel/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalE2E___SchemeModel"},"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Model.Composed/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Model___Composed":{"contents":"Paper › Symbolic/Specifications/Model › Composed.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the symbolic proof 13 headline theorems depend on it 108 of 219 lines trusted source ↗trust banner in the header: none; the closure computes B2 for the symbolic proofRead the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (10)class HasExecBytesinductive ComposedEventclass HasExecTraceinstance toTripleRatchetinstance toPQXDHSpqrdef aliceStartdef bobStartdef aliceStart.reachabilitydef bobStart.reachability#combine L192\n\nComposed Symbolic Protocol (PQXDH + Triple Ratchet)Composes the PQXDH handshake and threat transitions with the TripleRatchet messaging and state exposure transitions into a single DyLean state machine (Composed.reachability). aliceStart initializes Alice's TRState from PQXDH.aliceHandshake; bobStart atomically runs PQXDH.bobHandshake, initializes Bob's TRState, and decrypts the opening SignalMessage.\n\n\n\nclass HasExecBytesL58–61 ↗#Unified term algebra extending both TripleRatchet.HasExecBytes and PQXDH.HasExecBytes.\n\n\n\ninductive ComposedEventL71–74 ↗#Ghost event linking a Triple Ratchet session s to the trace index doneIdx of its PQXDHEvent.AliceDone or PQXDHEvent.BobDone event.\n\n\n\nclass HasExecTraceL80–91 ↗#Unified protocol trace carrying network messages, randomness, TREvent, PQXDHEvent, ComposedEvent, and compromisable TRState and PQXDHState stores.\n\n\n\ninstance toTripleRatchetL103–110 ↗#\n\ninstance toPQXDHSpqrL112–119 ↗#\n\n\n\ndef aliceStartL133–150 ↗#Alice's session initialization (process_prekey_bundle / initialize_alice_session): runs PQXDH.aliceHandshake, draws Alice's initial sending ratchet key dhsA, publishes the unauthenticated PreKeySignalMessage outer fields (ek, ct), logs AliceDone, InitSession, and HandshakeSession, and stores Alice's initial TRState. All application ciphertexts (including message 0) are sent separately via TripleRatchet.messageEncrypt.\n\ndef bobStartL152–173 ↗#Bob's atomic session initialization (message_decrypt_prekey): runs PQXDH.bobHandshake, constructs Bob's initial in-memory TRState (sid bound to both normalizeX25519Key msg.ratchetKey and keys.rk), and decrypts the inner SignalMessage via TripleRatchet.decryptInMemory. State and events (OPKUsed, BobDone, DHRatchet, HonestDH, HandshakeSession, skipped keys, Received, MessageKey) are committed only if decryption succeeds.\n\n\n\ndef aliceStart.reachabilityL182–185 ↗#\n\ndef bobStart.reachabilityL186–189 ↗#\n\n\n\n#combineL192–220 ↗#\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Symbolic/Specifications/Model/Composed.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Model.Composed/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Model___Composed"}});